              "question": "<p>The first beta blockers that came out (the first generation beta blockers) were non-selective. They blocked both the beta 1 and the beta 2 receptors. When the selective beta blockers came out, they were selective, hitting 'only' the beta 1 receptor. The major advantage of the second generation beta blockers over the first generation ones is that fact that they do not cause:&nbsp;</p>\n"
